# Copy to deploy/yeti/remote.env (git-ignored). Used by `npm run yeti -- …` (deploy/yeti/remote.sh).
# Dashboard → Node.js node → Web SSH ▾ → SSH tab shows the exact login, e.g. "ssh 12345-67890@gate.… -p 3022".
YETI_SSH="12345-67890@gate.ktm.yetiappcloud.com -p 3022"
# Optional: a specific private key (otherwise your default ~/.ssh key / ssh-agent)
# YETI_SSH_KEY_FILE=~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# Optional, first setup only: lets the server add its own read-only deploy key on GitHub
# (fine-grained token, this repository only, "Administration: Read and write"). Never commit it.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
